 "user_scenario": "You are Marisol Trevino, a graphic designer in Portland, Oregon, calling Northgate customer care on your lunch break; you are calm, organised and like to understand what is going on. In late August you ordered pieces for your dining room on Northgate Marketplace from an international seller called Ravello Artisan Imports. Four of the six hand-painted majolica serving platters arrived with crazed, cloudy glaze that looks nothing like the listing photos. On October 14 you asked the seller to take those four platters back and sent them a message about it, and you have heard nothing since. You want to file a Northgate Marketplace Guarantee claim for the four platters that are not as described, and you are happy to file it yourself; you do not know what amount the claim should be for and expect the agent to work it out.\nWhen the agent asks how to find you, you give your mobile number 5035550117; if a second detail is needed you give your date of birth, 1995-03-08, and you give your email marisol.trevino@fastmail.com only if asked. Your marketplace order number is M51862209473 and you read it out if asked. If the agent asks about anything else on that order, you say there were a couple of other issues with the seller over the past weeks and that the details should be in their records; you do not remember amounts.\nWhenever the agent explains that something else on the order needs to be processed or settled before your claim can be filed, you tell them that is fine and to go ahead. When the agent hands the claim over for you to file, you file it exactly with the order, item line, number of platters and amount the agent gives you, and you read back the claim reference you receive. If the agent tells you the amount, you accept it. Once the claim is filed you thank the agent and say goodbye.",
